cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "open-ml-notebooks: a book of 86 executed notebooks across machine learning, deep learning, and reinforcement learning"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lounissi
    given-names: Elyes
    email: pilot.tun@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1385-5070"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ELounissi/open-ml-notebooks"
url: "https://github.com/ELounissi/open-ml-notebooks"
abstract: >-
  A free book of 86 self-contained Jupyter notebooks covering machine learning,
  deep learning, and reinforcement learning, one method per notebook. Each
  chapter follows the same five parts: the idea in plain language, the maths, a
  minimal implementation from scratch, the library version annotated, and a
  measurement of where the method wins and where it loses. Every notebook ships
  already executed, so the charts, the printed tables, and the numbers are
  visible without running anything. Five open datasets are reused throughout, so
  results are directly comparable across chapters, and no claim in the prose
  appears unless the notebook printed it.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - deep learning
  - reinforcement learning
  - unsupervised learning
  - neural networks
  - jupyter notebooks
  - open datasets
  - reproducible research
  - machine learning tutorial
  - data science education
